01:31:14.760 --> 01:31:17.140
with the class that they have demonstrated

01:31:17.140 --> 01:31:21.770
for a promotion that will go down the annals

01:31:21.770 --> 01:31:24.150
of the history of the 1990s

01:31:24.150 --> 01:31:28.740
as being hardcore and being extreme

01:31:28.740 --> 01:31:29.960
and bringing blood.

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:36.440
back to the United States and crashing through tables and whacking each other with chairs and

01:31:36.440 --> 01:31:45.400
bringing a beer out to ringside and cursing on television and spitting on each other and defying

01:31:45.400 --> 01:31:52.000
all the rules and getting thrown off TV stations and being banned from pay-per-view. Look around

01:31:52.000 --> 01:31:58.700
and look at how the wrestlers have gone out and purchased suits and are wearing ties and have

01:31:58.700 --> 01:31:59.120
Yes.

01:32:07.710 --> 01:32:19.440
I mean, I'm sure Nujak had that hanging in his closet for all of his life, but I can guarantee you.

01:32:22.030 --> 01:32:29.400
But I know, I know for a personal fact that.

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:34.360
Sabu went out and bought that suit I know that the eliminators went out and

01:32:34.360 --> 01:32:38.960
bought their suits I know that almost every wrestler in this room tonight that

01:32:38.960 --> 01:32:43.840
is wearing a suit is wearing one strictly because they felt that this man

01:32:43.840 --> 01:32:49.780
who's on my left has made significant enough contributions to this industry

01:32:49.780 --> 01:32:54.980
that his presence here tonight warrants them putting on their best

01:33:04.640 --> 01:33:11.200
class that this room has demonstrated tonight demonstrates that what we do is

01:33:11.200 --> 01:33:18.260
what we do but that much like Terry Funk who has set the standard for us it's more

01:33:18.260 --> 01:33:22.830
than just being extreme it's more than just the image which we present there's

01:33:23.050 --> 01:33:29.260
a whole nother beam that's lying underneath all of us and

01:33:30.090 --> 01:33:33.190
I can't imitate Terry Funk as good as Chris Candido can.

01:33:34.550 --> 01:33:37.430
And I won't be up here as long as New Jack was.

01:33:38.250 --> 01:33:39.130
Thank God.

01:33:39.750 --> 01:33:40.230
And I'm right.

01:33:42.740 --> 01:33:44.040
I don't have to lie.

01:33:44.140 --> 01:33:45.120
I'll get my shit in his own.

01:33:57.070 --> 01:33:59.970
Y'all getting what you deserve right now.

01:34:00.000 --> 01:34:01.020
E.C.

01:34:01.180 --> 01:34:01.820
Motherfucker.

01:34:22.470 --> 01:34:29.980
I sat here tonight, and I listened to a lot of...

01:34:30.000 --> 01:34:37.230
people on Terry Funk's night be gracious enough to thank me for an opportunity which I was just a

01:34:37.230 --> 01:34:44.120
fan of theirs enough to present to them. Be it from Joey Stiles to the Eliminators to our referees

01:34:44.120 --> 01:34:53.900
to anybody. And before I come up here and tell you how much I believe in every single wrestler

01:34:53.900 --> 01:34:59.920
that's in this room and how much I'm a fan of every wrestler that's in this room and how much

01:35:00.700 --> 01:35:08.430
They mean, I'd like to tell you about a man that believed in me once, before anybody else did, before anybody else gave me a chance.

01:35:09.340 --> 01:35:15.090
See, I was a photographer, and I covered a Vern Gunn show in Minneapolis, Pro Wrestling USA show.

01:35:15.980 --> 01:35:20.480
And one of the people that was there in 1985 was Terry Funk, who did not like photographers.

01:35:21.520 --> 01:35:26.460
And I knew Paul Ellery, and I knew the Road Warriors, and I said, hey, you think maybe I'd get a couple pictures of Terry Funk?

01:35:26.660 --> 01:35:29.420
And Hawks are going, yeah, just go right up to him.

01:35:35.820 --> 01:35:39.740
And I'm kind of heading over his way and Jimmy Garvin, who I'd known from the New York City

01:35:39.740 --> 01:35:41.040
nightclub, he goes, where are you going?

01:35:41.160 --> 01:35:44.340
And I said, well, I'm going to go get a picture of Terry Funkin and Hawk said it was okay.

01:35:44.440 --> 01:35:45.440
And he goes, don't fucking do it.

01:35:47.520 --> 01:35:48.380
Don't fucking do it.

01:35:48.940 --> 01:35:52.040
He's going to chase around his dressing room and he's going to have a good time doing it.

01:35:52.140 --> 01:35:53.320
God help me if he catches it.

01:35:55.160 --> 01:35:58.740
And I went up to him and said, get the hell out of here, you son of a bitch.

01:35:58.900 --> 01:35:59.840
And he's chasing around.

01:36:03.660 --> 01:36:12.050
and I never saw him again until he came to Atlanta in 1989 and I was terrified of him

01:36:12.050 --> 01:36:15.370
as everybody else has told you tonight we're terrified of the guy

01:36:16.190 --> 01:36:18.950
and I was terrified he's like oh my gosh I came down and beat the shit

01:36:19.950 --> 01:36:22.230
I don't want to go to Atlanta and everybody's like hey man it's terrifying

01:36:22.230 --> 01:36:26.890
I just stayed away from him because I was terrified of him

01:36:26.890 --> 01:36:29.660
and we were

01:36:29.660 --> 01:36:29.860
wrong.

01:36:31.240 --> 01:36:34.460
We went to a show, and he wouldn't, he didn't even talk to me.

01:36:34.560 --> 01:36:38.860
I mean, it just, you know, I, I, how long is the fact that it's project being the same dressing user?

01:36:39.040 --> 01:36:40.760
Hello, Sonny, what the hell is her name again?

01:36:41.040 --> 01:36:41.460
You know?

01:36:42.260 --> 01:36:43.920
And we did a show in Amarillo.

01:36:45.680 --> 01:36:48.060
And I met Blue, his daughter.

01:36:49.620 --> 01:36:53.540
And Terry's walking around, he goes, so, he sits down next to me in this nightclub,

01:36:53.560 --> 01:36:57.100
and he says, so, Sonny, what do you think of Amarillo?

01:36:57.400 --> 01:36:59.700
And I'm from New York, and I go, well, you know, it's something.

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:01.040
It's a very nice place.

01:37:01.720 --> 01:37:04.200
I've never been here, and I don't know if I'm ever going to be back.

01:37:04.640 --> 01:37:05.840
I'm glad that you live here.

01:37:05.960 --> 01:37:06.940
I don't know what to say.

01:37:07.040 --> 01:37:07.940
I'm from New York.

01:37:08.380 --> 01:37:09.860
I've never been to Texas, you know?

01:37:10.420 --> 01:37:11.600
And he goes, that's a nice deal.

01:37:11.740 --> 01:37:13.160
You're riding with me tomorrow, by the way.

01:37:13.680 --> 01:37:14.720
You're riding with me tomorrow.

01:37:14.800 --> 01:37:15.300
We're going to talk.

01:37:15.520 --> 01:37:17.260
I'm like, oh, God, I'm going to ride with Terry Funk.

01:37:17.360 --> 01:37:18.140
He's going to pull out the side of the road.

01:37:18.200 --> 01:37:18.860
I did something.

01:37:19.000 --> 01:37:20.520
I'm going to beat the fucking shit out of me.

01:37:24.960 --> 01:37:28.420
So we're riding down the road, and he says, playing radio,

01:37:28.600 --> 01:37:29.870
and he's driving a 500.

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:35.540
miles an hour, and he's crazy and he's drinking a beer, and I'm like, oh my god, he's drinking

01:37:35.540 --> 01:37:39.120
a beer, and he's driving a Maxima, you know, Terry Rowan's like, shut the hell up, Sonny,

01:37:39.160 --> 01:37:43.900
I'm listening to the song, and I'm listening to the radio, and I'm sitting there, I'm going

01:37:43.900 --> 01:37:46.660
to learn about wrestling, and he's talking about country music, he's talking about Dusty

01:37:46.660 --> 01:37:52.260
Rose, he's talking about, you know, Amarillo, and his dad, and I can't get a wrestling story

01:37:52.260 --> 01:37:59.490
out of him, and I'm going, he's going to beat the shit out of me, so the night's over, and

01:37:59.490 --> 01:37:59.790
And, uh,

01:38:01.370 --> 01:38:05.230
We were going to separate towns, because there were only two towns at night, and he gives me his phone, and he goes,

01:38:05.310 --> 01:38:07.430
Hey, Sonny, call me. I want to talk to you. I want to talk to you.

01:38:08.090 --> 01:38:13.100
And I called his number, and Vicki answered the phone. Terry was out eating up a cow or something.

01:38:18.880 --> 01:38:22.760
And I said, Mrs. Funk, my name is Paul. And they called me Paul.

01:38:31.630 --> 01:38:35.160
I think you're just the funniest guy in TV!

01:38:40.230 --> 01:38:42.130
I'm not going to help you or lie, you'll kill me!

01:38:44.050 --> 01:38:47.950
And I said, well, it's a pleasure talking to you, Mrs. Funk, and just please don't, Terry.

01:38:48.090 --> 01:38:50.370
And I hung up the phone, and I was like, oh my god, oh my god, oh my god, oh my god.

01:38:50.470 --> 01:38:52.370
I said something wrong, and I was like, he's going to beat the hell out of me in the next show.

01:38:53.390 --> 01:38:58.420
Well, the next show was Memphis, and it was Eddie Gilbert against Terry Funk on top.

01:39:00.160 --> 01:39:04.650
And Eddie had Missy in his corner, and we were done.

01:39:04.870 --> 01:39:07.550
You know, I worked with the Samoan Swipe team, and we were done for the night.

01:39:07.710 --> 01:39:17.050
And I'm sitting in the back, and I got my shirt unbuttoned, and my belt's off, and I got my phone in my bag, and I have a Coke in my hand.

01:39:17.190 --> 01:39:22.960
And I'm sitting on the sofa, and all of a sudden, I hear, God damn, where the hell are you, sonny?

01:39:23.140 --> 01:39:23.920
Where the hell?

01:39:23.980 --> 01:39:25.940
And I'm like, where the fuck are you yelling at, man?

01:39:26.140 --> 01:39:27.580
Oh, yeah, where do you want to watch this match?

01:39:27.620 --> 01:39:28.620
And he grabs me by the hand.

01:39:28.680 --> 01:39:29.560
He goes, let's go.

01:39:29.680 --> 01:39:29.980
I go, go.

01:39:30.660 --> 01:39:32.420
We're going out to the ring!

01:39:32.640 --> 01:39:33.920
They go, what?!

01:39:37.010 --> 01:39:38.130
We're going out to the ring!

01:39:38.170 --> 01:39:39.270
No, I'm not going! I'm going!

01:39:39.470 --> 01:39:40.050
No, no!

01:39:41.950 --> 01:39:45.030
And he's walking out like this

01:39:45.030 --> 01:39:49.230
and I'm going, here man, I'm managing Terry Funk!

01:39:49.370 --> 01:39:50.330
I don't deserve this!

01:39:50.670 --> 01:39:52.520
And Flair's going to kill me

01:39:52.520 --> 01:39:53.800
when he finds out about it!

01:39:55.260 --> 01:39:57.260
So, we get out to the ring

01:39:57.260 --> 01:39:59.090
and then he's there with Missy

01:39:59.090 --> 01:39:59.970
and I look at him, you know, and...

01:40:00.520 --> 01:40:29.690
And Eddie and I were so tight, I said, I look out, I don't know what the fuck you're doing here either, you know, and Missy's doing her nails, and I go, what the fuck am I doing, and he gets on the mic and he goes, Holly, I'm going to tell you this once, if that douchebag.

01:40:30.000 --> 01:40:48.580
gets in your way, slap the fucking piss out of her. And he puts down the mic and he goes, I'm fucking shooting too. Oh my god, oh my god, I'm gonna have to beat up Missy and if I don't, he's gonna beat me up, I'm dead, I'm dead, I'm dead, I'm dead, I'm dead.

01:40:51.890 --> 01:40:59.830
So, they have this whole elaborate thing set up and Terry's climbing the rails and he's chasing after the fans and

01:41:00.090 --> 01:41:29.580
And he's chasing after me, and I'm like, I'm your manager, I'm your manager, and he's chasing after Missy, and he's beating up Eddie, and Terry goes to the top rope, and he has this whole thing that he has in his mind, and I'm just sitting around, and Eddie's on the canvas, and Terry goes to the top rope, and he goes like this, and like this, and I'm going, wow, look at this, man, this is Terry Funk, man, this is Terry Funk in action, and he's, whoa, whoa.

01:41:31.850 --> 01:41:36.450
And all of a sudden, he stands up straight, puts his hands by his side, he goes, fuck it, I can't keep my balance.

01:41:36.470 --> 01:41:41.280
And he falls off, and he goes straight through the table at ringside, head first.

01:41:43.900 --> 01:41:46.780
And I'm sitting there going, wow, I don't remember hearing about this.

01:41:51.160 --> 01:41:53.080
That pretty fucking impressive.

01:41:55.540 --> 01:41:59.340
I look up at Eddie, and I go, wow, he goes, fuck over there, he's dead!

01:42:05.280 --> 01:42:09.300
I'm thinking, oh man, Flair's gonna kick my fucking ass.

01:42:09.660 --> 01:42:11.370
He's gonna think it was mine, right?

01:42:11.650 --> 01:42:13.550
And I go over there, and he's just, and he's there,

01:42:13.590 --> 01:42:15.520
and he's dead, and he's lying there.

01:42:15.900 --> 01:42:17.760
He's lying there, and he's not even doing this stuff.

01:42:17.860 --> 01:42:20.040
He's dead. He's motionless.

01:42:20.080 --> 01:42:22.780
And I go, I cup his neck, and now I'm crying,

01:42:22.900 --> 01:42:24.460
because I figure he's dead, and I'm dead,

01:42:24.520 --> 01:42:25.320
and we're all dead.

01:42:25.580 --> 01:42:28.140
And I look up, and I go, he's dead, and he's dead.

01:42:28.260 --> 01:42:28.980
And he goes, I know he's dead.

01:42:30.000 --> 01:42:38.870
And I go, Terry, Terry, you okay, Terry, squeeze me, Terry, squeeze my hand, Terry, do something, he goes, you know, I don't have that many bumps like that left in me.

01:42:41.980 --> 01:42:59.780
And he got up and he beat the shit out of all of us that night and put on a show that today.

01:43:00.000 --> 01:43:08.560
day was awe-inspiring. I rode with him for the next week, and a week later is when he

01:43:08.560 --> 01:43:15.740
broke his tailbone. And now the whole room goes, you know, I mean, this is where the story

01:43:15.740 --> 01:43:22.580
gets heavy. And this is the story of ECW. Terry broke his tailbone in Macon, Georgia,

01:43:23.880 --> 01:43:29.980
and I was fortunate enough to ride with him to Savannah that night, and I had...

01:43:30.030 --> 01:43:35.530
I had heard stories about his toughness, and I had heard stories about how raw-boned he was.

01:43:36.990 --> 01:43:42.050
He's in the car, and I'm looking over, and I saw tears going down his face, and he wouldn't acknowledge it.

01:43:42.790 --> 01:43:43.430
I said, jeez.

01:43:48.530 --> 01:43:51.590
Right before we pulled into Savannah, he turned to me and goes, I'm goddamn hurt.

01:43:53.080 --> 01:43:53.920
Fuck, I'm hurt.

01:43:54.560 --> 01:43:57.980
And this was three weeks before the Great American Dance in Baltimore with him and Flair.

01:43:59.700 --> 01:43:59.840
End.

01:44:00.060 --> 01:44:05.140
It scared me because I never heard Terry Funk acknowledge that he was hurting.

01:44:05.900 --> 01:44:08.760
He broke his ass, literally broke his ass.

01:44:09.000 --> 01:44:10.260
He broke his tailbone.

01:44:10.540 --> 01:44:16.060
So I took him to the hospital the next morning, and he didn't want to go.

01:44:16.510 --> 01:44:18.880
And I said, Terry, you gotta go, bro, you gotta go.

01:44:20.840 --> 01:44:27.040
I took him to the hospital, and the x-rayed him, and the doctor came in the room and he said,

01:44:27.180 --> 01:44:28.880
Mr. Funk, you have a broken sacrum.

01:44:30.090 --> 01:44:34.750
broken your tailbone. You'll be okay. You'll be back in the ring in about nine

01:44:34.750 --> 01:44:42.590
months to a year." He says, I have a match on pay-per-view in three weeks. And the

01:44:42.590 --> 01:44:49.220
doctor says, if I have to admit you in this hospital, you don't have a match in

01:44:49.220 --> 01:44:59.970
three weeks. Forget it. In a year, maybe. The doctor left the room, I looked at him, and he...

01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:01.510
He was devastated.

01:45:03.340 --> 01:45:04.120
And I said, it's the pain.

01:45:04.200 --> 01:45:04.600
He goes, nope.

01:45:05.830 --> 01:45:07.290
I said, it's the fact that you can't wrestle.

01:45:07.430 --> 01:45:08.070
He said, nope.

01:45:09.760 --> 01:45:12.610
I said, is it because you think they're going to screw you over?

01:45:12.770 --> 01:45:13.350
He said, nope.

01:45:13.990 --> 01:45:14.770
I said, what is it?

01:45:15.330 --> 01:45:20.770
And he said, there are people who, in three weeks from now, are paying to see me work with

01:45:20.770 --> 01:45:23.680
Ric Flair, and they're expecting a hell of a match.

01:45:24.740 --> 01:45:29.760
And I'll be goddamned if a doctor or a broken ass or anybody on the face of this planet

01:45:29.760 --> 01:45:29.940
Thank you.

01:45:30.250 --> 01:45:34.010
God himself is going to stop me from getting into that ring in Baltimore

01:45:34.010 --> 01:45:36.930
and giving the people his show that they paid to see.

01:45:37.230 --> 01:45:42.620
The man had an elbow that was puffed out to here.

01:45:42.860 --> 01:45:43.680
They drained it.

01:45:43.780 --> 01:45:45.100
His knees were swelling.

01:45:45.200 --> 01:45:46.220
He was wearing knee braces.

01:45:46.420 --> 01:45:50.840
They were working him on the road 34 straight days that month.

01:45:51.190 --> 01:45:54.970
Double shots against Sting, against Eddie Gilbert, against the Steiner brothers.

01:45:55.190 --> 01:45:58.490
Every baby face in that promotion was programmed against him.

01:45:58.590 --> 01:45:59.970
And they were drawing money for...

01:46:00.250 --> 01:46:18.880
He was carrying the promotion on his back, he broke his ass, and the only thing that was going through his mind was the fact that the people paid to see him do his thing, and he would be damned if anything would stop him.

01:46:35.180 --> 01:46:37.800
That night, I called my father on the phone.

01:46:39.690 --> 01:46:43.440
My father, who is one of the hardest-working men I've ever known,

01:46:44.060 --> 01:46:46.720
I said, Dad, I met somebody who has that same work ethic.

01:46:47.610 --> 01:46:49.710
I met somebody who loves what he does.

01:46:50.300 --> 01:46:53.360
I met somebody who takes such pride in what he does

01:46:53.360 --> 01:46:55.820
and the fact that people have believed in him,

01:46:55.980 --> 01:46:59.400
that he cares that much, that he'll make this type of sacrifice.

01:47:00.060 --> 01:47:02.060
for the people who paid to see him.

01:47:04.100 --> 01:47:09.810
On that night in 1989, I prayed that I would find one,

01:47:10.180 --> 01:47:12.640
let alone a dressing room full of wrestlers,

01:47:12.880 --> 01:47:14.880
who would have that same work ethic,

01:47:15.580 --> 01:47:17.920
who would take that tradition to the next level.

01:47:18.530 --> 01:47:20.750
And I looked around that dressing room in WCW,

01:47:20.810 --> 01:47:22.850
